                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pray for Death is a game that I never even heard of back in the day because it was only on PC. Which is too bad because it feels pretty similar to Killer Instinct Gold, and it would have made for a great N64 game to play at sleepovers. \n\nThe game is really cheesy which I like, and the gameplay is okay, yeah it’s similar to Killer Instinct Gold, but a very rough around the edges KI Gold. I’d like to see a remaster of this game just with smoothed out gameplay, updated graphics, and online play. Just as long as they kept all of the cheesiness intact.\n\nThe Dollary Doo Factor. My biggest complaint about this game is the price, 10 dollary doos is way too much, and in the rare instances it goes on sale, it never drops below 7 dollary doos. A 1 dollary doo sale price a couple of times a year would do wonders, it’s hard to get mad at something you only spent 1 dollary doo on.\n\nThe Community Hub for this game is pretty bare at the moment, so I slapped together [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2909274752]PRAY FOR DEATH MOVE LIST GUIDE[/url]. \n\nAlso, Pantera is bae.",
